 ---------------------------------------------------
  
 *--------------------------------------------------*
  Case2 : When ponding just starts 
 *--------------------------------------------------*
 *                                                  *
 *   t  = Rainfall duration                         *
 *   tp = Time required for ponding to occur after  *
 *        rain starts at t = 0;                     *
 *   fp = Infiltrate depth at ponding in cm         *
 * infp = Infiltrate rate at ponding in cm/hr       *
 *--------------------------------------------------*
  
     tp    in minutes     =    15.291870
     tp    in hours       =      .25
     fp    in cm          =     1.0195
     infp  in cm/hr       =     4.0000
 *------------------------------------------------*
  
 Note:
  
 Please, check the values of (fp & infp) as obtained
 above [in Case 2] against the results below       
 [in Case 3] in (cloumn 3 & column 4), when t = tp;
  
  
 *--------------------------------------------------*
 Case 3 : Under Constant Rainfall Intensity(i)
 *-------------------------------------------------*
 * 1st column = t (rainfall duration) in hours     *
 * 2nd column = t (rainfall duration) in minutes   *
 * 3rd column = f (cumulative infiltration) in cm  *
 * 4th column = inf (infiltration rate) in cm/hr   *
 *-------------------------------------------------*
  
     .17      10        .5981       6.0498
     .33      20       1.3055       3.3623
     .50      30       1.8060       2.7326
     .67      40       2.2329       2.4186
     .83      50       2.6186       2.2229
    1.00      60       2.9771       2.0865
    1.17      70       3.3160       1.9846
    1.33      80       3.6399       1.9050
    1.50      90       3.9519       1.8407
    1.67     100       4.2541       1.7874
    1.83     110       4.5481       1.7423
    2.00     120       4.8352       1.7036
    2.17     130       5.1162       1.6698
    2.33     140       5.3920       1.6402
    2.50     150       5.6631       1.6138
    2.67     160       5.9301       1.5903
    2.83     170       6.1934       1.5690
    3.00     180       6.4532       1.5497
 *------------------------------------------------*
  
 Some Observations are : 
  
 When ponding just starts(at t= tp): 
 ----------------------------------- 
 infp = inf = i   &   fp = f [as in Case 2 & Case 3]
 where i= input rainfall intensity.
  
  
 Any (-) ve values of (f &/or inf), in the begining
 time steps, indicates "No infiltration" 
  
 Like rate & duration of rainfall(as input data), the
 rate & duration of irrigated also may be considered.
  
 *------------------------------------------------*
  
  
 Some factors overlooked here are :
  
 Vegetation cover, Air confinement ahead of the
 wetting front, Surface roughness, Plant roots etc;
  
 these retard the flow & creat additional pore spaces
 so infiltration & K (Hydraulic conductivity) of
 the soil increases!
  
